  "post": {
    "caption": "Elton John's kneecaps became a necklace. After Elton John had both knees replaced, he asked his surgeon if he could keep the kneecaps. The surgeon was rather startled, and told him he had never operated on worse knees. Elton gave the bones to his friend, the jeweler Theo Fennell, whose team baked them dry and polished them. The right kneecap became a necklace on a chain of bone, and the smaller left one became a brooch. The back carries a Latin phrase about bowing to no man. He showed them in a World Gold Council film in 2025.",
